# groups1 — consumer groups: XGROUP, XREADGROUP, XACK
#
# Learn: a consumer group lets several workers share one stream: each
# entry goes to one consumer, and stays "pending" for it until it's
# acknowledged with XACK. XGROUP CREATE key group <id> sets where the
# group starts: $ means "only entries added from now on", 0 means "from
# the very beginning". MKSTREAM creates the stream if it's missing.
#
# Task: the stream events already holds 3 signups that still need a
# welcome mail. Create the group mailer so it will see them, let consumer
# w1 read 2 entries, and acknowledge the first one
# (1700000000000-0), which was mailed successfully.
#

XGROUP CREATE events mailer $
XREADGROUP GROUP mailer w1 COUNT 2 STREAMS events >
XACK events mailer 1700000000000-0
